          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            = succeed "," do
              %em rigid (monoidal) category
            %em autonomous (monoidal) category
            is a kind of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+with+duals"} category with duals
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
            in which every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            has a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dual+object"} dual object
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^*
          %p
            Depending on whether these duals exist on the right or the left we call the category
            %em left rigid
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %em right rigid
            %em rigid
            refers to categories with duals on both sides.
          %p
            It is important to note that every right/left rigid category can be fully embedded into a category with duals on both sides, by repeatedly applying the double dual functor and taking a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
            (see e.g.
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Selinger2011"} Selinger 2011
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
            is
            %strong right rigid
            (or right autonomous) if every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
            has a right
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dualizable+object"} dual
            %strong left rigid
            (or left autonomous) if every object has a left dual. A monoidal category is autonomous (sometimes called rigid) if duals exist on both sides.
          %p
            Conventions differ regarding which type of duals are which. One convention is as follows: a
            %em right dual
            of an object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            in a monoidal category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi.mathscript 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathscr{C}
            is an object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^*
            equipped with evaluation/co-evaluation maps
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mtext ev
                    %mi A
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo ⊗
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mo *
                  %mo →
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mtext coev
                    %mi A
                  %mo :
                  %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mo *
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \text{ev}_{A}:A\otimes A^*\to 1,\,\, \text{coev}_{A}:1\to A^*\otimes A
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            is the tensor unit, subject to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/triangle+identities"} triangle identities
            (snake diagrams)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mtext ev
                    %mi A
                  %mo ⊗
                  %msub
                    %mtext id
                    %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∘
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mtext id
                    %mi A
                  %mo ⊗
                  %msub
                    %mtext coev
                    %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mtext id
                    %mi A
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\text{ev}_A\otimes \text{id}_A)\circ (\text{id}_A\otimes \text{coev}_{A})=\text{id}_{A},
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mtext id
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi A
                        %mo *
                  %mo ⊗
                  %msub
                    %mtext ev
                    %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∘
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mtext coev
                    %mi A
                  %mo ⊗
                  %msub
                    %mtext id
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi A
                        %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mtext id
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi A
                        %mo *
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\text{id}_{A^*}\otimes \text{ev}_{A})\circ ( \text{coev}_{A}\otimes \text{id}_{A^*})=\text{id}_{A^*}.
          %p
            A left dual is an object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^*
            paired with morphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mtext ev
                    %mi A
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mo *
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \text{ev}_A:A^*\otimes A\to 1
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mtext coev
                    %mi A
                  %mo :
                  %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                  %mo ⊗
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \text{coev}_A:1\to A\otimes A^*
            satisfying the dual conditions.
          %h2#examples Examples
          %p
            The canonical example of a rigid category is the category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mtext Vec
                    %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \text{Vec}_k
            of finite dimensional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector spaces
            over a field
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            the standard dual
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi V
                    %mo *
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mtext Hom
                    %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ,
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V^*=\text{Hom}_k(V,k)
            serves as a categorical dual for
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
          %p
          .num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              be a field. For every vector space
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mtext Vec
                        %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V\in \text{Vec}_k
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mtext ev
                      %mi V
                    %mo :
                    %mi V
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msup
                      %mi V
                      %mo *
                    %mo →
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \text{ev}_V: V\otimes V^*\to k
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi v
                    %mo ,
                    %mi φ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi φ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi v
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (v,\varphi)\mapsto \varphi(v)
            %p and
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mtext coev
                      %mi V
                    %mo :
                    %mi k
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi V
                      %mo *
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \text{coev}_V: k\to V^*\otimes V
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi x
                    %mo ⋅
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                    %msub
                      %mi φ
                      %mi i
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\mapsto x\cdot \sum_{i\in I}\varphi_i\otimes v_i
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{v_i\}_{i\in I}
              is a basis for
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi φ
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varphi_i
              is a dual basis. That is,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi φ
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varphi_i
              is defined by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi φ
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mrow
                        %mtable{:columnalign => "left left", :displaystyle => "false"}
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mn 1
                            %mtd
                              %mi i
                              %mo =
                              %mi j
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mn 0
                            %mtd
                              %mtext otherwise
                              %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\varphi_i(v_j)=
                    \\begin{cases}
                    1 &amp; i=j\\
                    0 &amp; \text{otherwise}.
                    \\end{cases}
            %p
              These formulas give well defined
              = succeed "-morphisms." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mtext Vec
                        %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \text{Vec}_k
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mtext Vec
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \text{Vec}_k
              the structure of a (right) rigid category.
          %p
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              To begin, we verify that the definition of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mtext coev
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \text{coev}
              is independent of basis. Suppose
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi v
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\tilde{v}_i\}_{i\in I}
              is a different choice of basis. There is a change of basis matrix
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ,
                        %mi j
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi i
                        %mo ,
                        %mi j
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                        %mo ×
                        %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c=(c_{i,j})_{(i,j)\in I\times I}
              between them. It is straightforward to see that the dual bases are related by the change of basis matrix
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi c
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c^{-1}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi v
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mi i
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi φ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mi i
                    %mo =
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mi i
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                        %mi j
                      %msub
                        %mi c
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo ,
                          %mi j
                      %mo ⋅
                      %msub
                        %mi v
                        %mi i
                      %mo )
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                        %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi c
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mrow
                          %mi k
                          %mo ,
                          %mi i
                      %mo ⋅
                      %msub
                        %mi φ
                        %mi i
                      %mo )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sum_{i}\tilde{v}_i\otimes \tilde{\varphi}_i=\sum_{i}\left(\sum_{j}c_{i,j}\cdot v_i\right)\otimes \left(\sum_{k}(c^{-1})_{k,i}\cdot \varphi_i\right)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo =
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi j
                        %mo ,
                        %mi k
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                        %mi i
                      %msub
                        %mi c
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo ,
                          %mi j
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi c
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mrow
                          %mi k
                          %mo ,
                          %mi i
                      %mo )
                    %mo ⋅
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mi i
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msub
                      %mi φ
                      %mi i
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} =\sum_{j,k} \left(\sum_{i}c_{i,j}(c^{-1})_{k,i}\right)\cdot v_i\otimes \varphi_i.
            %p
              The definition of the inverse matrix says that
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                        %mi i
                      %msub
                        %mi c
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo ,
                          %mi j
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi c
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mrow
                          %mi k
                          %mo ,
                          %mi i
                      %mo =
                      %mrow
                        %mo {
                        %mrow
                          %mtable{:columnalign => "left left", :displaystyle => "false"}
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mn 1
                              %mtd
                                %mi j
                                %mo =
                                %mi k
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mn 0
                              %mtd
                                %mtext otherwise
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sum_{i}c_{i,j}(c^{-1})_{k,i}=\begin{cases}1 &amp; j=k \\ 0 &amp;\text{otherwise}\end{cases}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi v
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mi i
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi φ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mi i
                    %mo =
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mi i
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msub
                      %mi φ
                      %mi i
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sum_{i}\tilde{v}_i\otimes \tilde{\varphi}_i=\sum_{i}v_i\otimes \varphi_i,
            %p
              so
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} coev
                      %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \coev_{V}
              is well defined as desired. We now show that the rigidity diagrams commute. Going around the square, we find that this is equivalent to the condition that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi w
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi φ
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi w
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1\otimes w=\sum_{i}\varphi_i(w)\otimes v_i
              for all
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi w
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w\in V
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mi i
                    %mo =
                    %mi w
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v_i=w
              for some
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi φ
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi w
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mi i
                    %mo =
                    %mi w
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varphi_i(w)\otimes v_i=w
              and all the other terms are zero, making the equality obvious.
          %p
            Another key example is that of endofunctor categories. Given any category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi.mathscript 𝒞
