          %h3#free_rigid_monoidal_categories Free rigid monoidal categories
          %p
            The inclusion of the 2-category of monoidal categories into the 2-category of rigid monoidal categories admits a left
            %span.newWikiWord
              2-adjoint functor
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/2-adjoint+functor"} ?
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
          %p
            Furthermore, the unit of the adjunction is a strong monoidal
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fully+faithful+functor"} fully faithful functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            admits a fully faithful strong monoidal functor
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C\to L(C)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L(C)
            is a rigid monoidal category.
          %p
            See Theorems 1 and 2 in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Delpeuch"} Delpeuch
